.TH MELOSD 1 "2026-11-19" "melos 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
melosd \- resident daemon for the melos music player
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B melosd
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B melosd
owns playback, the library index, local source scanning, lyrics cache,
listening statistics, media downloads, and the MPRIS interface for
.BR melos (1).
It listens on a Unix socket and accepts newline-delimited JSON commands from
clients.
.PP
Normally the TUI starts the daemon on demand. It can also be started by systemd
socket activation with the user unit
.IR melos.socket ,
or directly. One instance per user is supported.
.PP
The daemon spawns a warm
.BR mpv (1)
process, so the first track starts without waiting for a player to boot.
Playback continues when all clients detach. The daemon exits when it receives
.B Shutdown
from a client, SIGTERM, or SIGINT.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Read configuration from
.IR PATH
instead of
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/melos/config.toml .
.TP
.BI \-\-music\-dir " DIR"
Override the configured managed music directory.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.SH SYSTEMD
The package provides
.I melos.socket
and
.I melos.service
as user units. Enable socket activation with:
.PP
.nf
.RS
systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now melos.socket
.RE
.fi
.PP
The units are not enabled automatically. Without them, the TUI starts
.B melosd
itself and writes its output to
.IR ~/.local/state/melos/daemon.log .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/melos/config.toml
Configuration, including download and mpv options.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/melos/library.db
SQLite index of tracks, sources, playlists, lyrics, and listening statistics.
Audio files are the source of truth; the index can be rebuilt by rescanning
your sources.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/melos/state.json
Persisted queue, position, volume, shuffle, and repeat state. Written
atomically on track changes and periodically while playing.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/melos/daemon.log
Output from a daemon spawned by the TUI.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/melos/download\-N.log
yt-dlp stderr for each download job, kept for troubleshooting.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/melos/art
Embedded or nearby cover art extracted from tracks and cached for the
interface.
.TP
.I ~/Music/melos
Managed library for downloads and copied imports.
.TP
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR /melos/daemon.sock
Client socket, mode 0600.
.TP
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR /melos/mpv.sock
Private mpv IPC socket.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LISTEN_FDS " / " LISTEN_PID
Used by systemd socket activation. When exactly one socket is passed, the
daemon uses it instead of binding its own.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Log filter, for example
.BR melosd=debug .
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " XDG_DATA_HOME ", " XDG_STATE_HOME ", " XDG_CACHE_HOME ", " XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
XDG base directories.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on clean shutdown, non-zero if the socket cannot be bound, the database
cannot be opened, or another instance is already running.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR melos (1),
.BR mpv (1),
.BR yt\-dlp (1),
.BR systemd.socket (5)
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/ZT-Things/melos/issues.
